es-clock-management-college-football","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"CFB Week 12 best bets: Breaking down the numbers for Texas Tech, Kentucky and more","description":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno break down the best bets they see around college football for Week 12.","published":"2026-11-19T11:45:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50513003/college-football-odds-best-bets-week-12-spreads-lines-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"South Carolina star QB LaNorris Sellers set to play vs. No. 1 Georgia","description":"South Carolina star QB LaNorris Sellers is set to play in Saturday's game vs. No. 1 Georgia after not appearing on the injury report Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-19T03:01:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50526154/south-carolina-qb-lanorris-sellers-set-play-vs-georgia","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NC State names NFL assistant Jason Michael as OC under Philip Rivers","published":"2026-11-19T12:21:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50524698/nc-state-names-nfl-assistant-michael-oc-rivers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia AG asks SEC to take action against LSU's 'contempt for the rules'","description":"The Georgia Attorney General blasted LSU in a letter to SEC commissioner Greg Sankey, encouraging sanctions against the Tigers, \"up to and including expulsion.\"","published":"2026-11-19T04:59:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50524054/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870736/mark-fletcher-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Fletcher_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Mark Fletcher Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Fletcher_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:32Z","intro":"Mark Fletcher Jr. (born October 17, 2004) is an American college football running back for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Fletcher attended American Heritage School in Plantation, Florida. As a senior, he rushed for 1,934 yards and 23 touchdowns. Fletcher originally committed to Ohio State, before decommitting during his senior year. A four-star recruit, he committed to play college football at the University of Miami over an offer from Florida."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Fletcher made his Hurricanes debut in the 2023 season opener against Miami (Ohio), rushing for 76 yards on nine carries and a touchdown in a 38–3 victory. Against Virginia, he scored the game-winning touchdown in overtime in a 29–26 win. Against NC State, he rushed for 115 yards, marking his first 100-yard collegiate game, in a 20–6 loss. He ran for a season-high 126 yards and two touchdowns against Louisville in a 38–31 defeat. In the 2023 Pinstripe Bowl, Fletcher suffered a Lisfranc injury and was carted off the field. He finished his freshman season with 514 rushing yards and five touchdowns in ten games and four starts, missing three games due to other injuries.\nFletcher returned from injury for the 2024 season, playing in all 13 games and making four starts. He made an immediate impact in the season opener against Florida, rushing for two touchdowns in a 41–17 victory.\nIn 2025, Fletcher had back‑to‑back games with two rushing touchdowns in Miami’s victories over Bethune–Cookman and South Florida in Weeks 2 and 3. He recorded a career‑high three rushing touchdowns and 106 yards on 23 carries in a 42–7 win against Stanford. In the first round of the College Football Playoff against Texas A&M, Fletcher rushed for a career‑high 172 yards on 17 carries in a 10–3 victory. In the quarterfinal against Ohio State, he ran for 90 yards on 19 carries and was named the J. Curtis Sanford Offensive Most Valuable Player as the Hurricanes won 24–14. Fletcher continued his strong postseason run in the semifinal against Ole Miss, rushing for 133 yards on 22 carries in a 31–27 win. In the 2026 College Football Playoff National Championship against Indiana, Fletcher rushed for 112 yards and two touchdowns, including a career-long 57-yard score, in a 27–21 defeat. On the field after the game, he threw a punch at Indiana defensive lineman Tyrique Tucker. Fletcher finished the 2025 season having played in 14 games with 12 starts, rushing for an ACC‑leading 1,192 yards on 216 carries with a 5.5 average and 12 touchdowns, and was named third-team All-ACC."}]}}